// Fleet Foot Fighter

@100 = ~Fleet Foot Fighter~
@101 = ~Fleet Foot Fighter~
@102 = ~FLEET FOOT FIGHTER: Barefoot and grinning, the Fleet Foot is gone before the blade falls. Raised on the hedge-lanes and orchard runs of halfling villages, these duellists never learned to stand still: they dart between legs, vault tables and leave only a blur where they stood. Bigger folk call it cheating. The Fleet Foot calls it a fair fight.

Advantages:
– +2 AC at level 1, plus +1 every 5 levels afterwards.
– Small Target: +2 AC against missiles, rising to +4 at level 10.
– Fleet of Foot: +2 movement at level 1, plus +1 every 2 levels afterwards.
– Weapon speed improves by 1 at level 1, and by 1 more every 5 levels afterwards.
– +1/2 attack per round at level 1, and again at level 19.
– Starts with 2 slots in Two-Weapon Style.
– May reach grandmastery in daggers, short swords, katanas and quarterstaffs.
– Razor's Edge: every melee hit with a dagger, short sword or katana opens a wound that bleeds for 3 rounds: 1 damage per round at level 1, rising by 1 every 10 levels. Wounds stack. Undead, golems, elementals and slimes do not bleed.
– From level 7: Rapid Strike once per day, plus once more every 4 levels afterwards.
  RAPID STRIKE: Doubles attacks per round for 4 rounds, plus 1 round every 5 levels afterwards, at a penalty to hit that shrinks from -4 to nothing by level 19.

Disadvantages:
– Cannot wear armour, helmets or boots, or use shields.
– May only use daggers (including throwing daggers), short swords, katanas and quarterstaffs.
– Must be a halfling.~

@110 = ~Fleet Foot~
@111 = ~The Fleet Foot's speed, footwork and quick hands.~

@120 = ~Rapid Strike~
@121 = ~Rapid Strike

Doubles the Fleet Foot's attacks per round, and its movement with them, for 4 rounds at level 7, plus 1 round every 5 levels afterwards. Attacks suffer a penalty to hit of -4 at level 7, -3 at 10, -2 at 13 and -1 at 16, and none from level 19. Does not combine with Haste or Improved Haste.~
@122 = ~Rapid Strike~

@130 = ~Razor's Edge~
@131 = ~Razor's Edge

A bleeding wound: 1 damage per round for 3 rounds, rising by 1 for every 10 of the Fleet Foot's levels.~

@140 = ~Flicker Step~
@141 = ~Flicker Step

The Fleet Foot steps out of time for about 7 seconds. It can move freely while everyone else is frozen, but cannot attack or cast until the effect ends.~

@145 = ~Time Slow~
@146 = ~Time Slow

Stops time for everyone but the Fleet Foot for 1 round.~

@150 = ~Time Pause~
@151 = ~Time Pause

Stops time for everyone but the Fleet Foot for 2 rounds.~

@155 = ~Afterimage~
@156 = ~Afterimage

For 1 turn, the Fleet Foot leaves 4 blurred copies of itself that work like Mirror Image. This is a physical ability, so it cannot be dispelled.~

@160 = ~Relentless~
@161 = ~Relentless

The Fleet Foot can no longer be held, paralysed, slowed, webbed, entangled, stunned or frightened. From level 30 it also gains +10% resistance to physical damage.~

@165 = ~Hamstring~
@166 = ~Hamstring

For 1 round, every hit hamstrings the target for 2 rounds: -1 attack per round, -2 to hit and half movement. There is no save, and Free Action doesn't help, since it is a wound rather than magic. Further hits refresh the wound but do not stack.~
@167 = ~Hamstrung~

@170 = ~Quicksilver~
@171 = ~Quicksilver

Each time this ability is chosen, the Fleet Foot gains +10% magic resistance. It simply isn't where the spell was aimed.~

@175 = ~Fleet Training~
@176 = ~Fleet Training

Each time this ability is chosen, the Fleet Foot gains +1 movement.~

@180 = ~Fleet Foot Fighters cannot use this item.~
